l,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-09-21T06:31:33Z","updated_at":"2025-09-21T14:25:33Z","closed_at":"2025-09-21T14:25:28Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.4.1 (stable) — reproducible\n\n4.5 (stable) — reproducible\n\nNo custom build. Also reproducible in a clean project.\n\n### System information\n\nwindows 11, RTX 3080 , AMD Ryzen 3950X , 128GB RAM \n\n### Issue description\n\nI’m testing human animations retargeted onto a robot skeleton.\nWhen I play the animation in the editor preview (without running the scene), it looks fine at first, but after some time the animation starts to stutter.\n\nIf I press F6 and run the scene, there’s no stutter (the animation is perfectly smooth).\nInterestingly, if I enable the Loop option for the animation, the editor stutter disappears as well.\n\nExpected: Editor preview should play as smoothly as when running the scene (F6).\nActual: Editor preview sometimes stutters after initial playback; running the scene or enabling Loop removes the stutter.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0f86d6ec-6eba-41d0-b2d5-a25c013e548b\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3ded2c7e-5cc2-4418-b9a8-b28c02b08a29\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n\n<img width=\"2174\" height=\"1127\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9f854b44-4cf8-48cd-af25-91d31b0fde0f\" />\n\nEditor  Animation Play Vs   F6 Run    (KEY_2,KEY_3 Press)\n\nReproducible project\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[editor-animation-problem.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22450142/editor-animation-problem.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id"